<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Penedès</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Penedès is a historic region of Catalonia between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarragona">Tarragona</a>, divided into the comarques of Alt Penedès, Baix Penedès and Garraf. In antiquity it was home to the Iberian Cessetani, and in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it was a frontier march of the county of Barcelona. It is known for its wines, especially the cava produced around Sant Sadurní d'<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anoia">Anoia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/penedes.jpg" alt="Penedès" width="320" height="311" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vilarrubla · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pened%C3%A8s_region_and_DO.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
